import{_ as t,c as o,b as r,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.BEqfOpL-.js";const i="/images/find_competitors.webp",m=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Competitor Finder","description":"Competitor Finder identifies podcasts competing for the same audience as your show — based on search rankings, platform recommendations, genre overlap, and visibility — not just by category. Instead of a flat list, it ranks competitors by how much of a competitive threat they pose, so you can see at a glance who's worth watching and who's worth tracking.","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"features/competitor-finder.md","filePath":"features/competitor-finder.md"}`),s={name:"features/competitor-finder.md"};function n(l,e,c,p,h,d){return r(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="competitor-finder" tabindex="-1">Competitor Finder <a class="header-anchor" href="#competitor-finder" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Competitor Finder&quot;">​</a></h1><h2 id="discover-the-podcasts-really-fighting-for-your-audience" tabindex="-1">Discover the Podcasts Really Fighting for Your Audience <a class="header-anchor" href="#discover-the-podcasts-really-fighting-for-your-audience" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Discover the Podcasts Really Fighting for Your Audience&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Competitor Finder identifies podcasts competing for the same audience as your show — based on search rankings, platform recommendations, genre overlap, and visibility — not just by category. Instead of a flat list, it ranks competitors by how much of a competitive threat they pose, so you can see at a glance who&#39;s worth watching and who&#39;s worth tracking.</p><p><a href="/images/find_competitors.webp" title="Open screenshot at full size"><img src="'+i+'" alt="Competitor Finder Interface" width="600px" style="display:block;margin:0 auto;"></a></p><p><strong>To access:</strong> <strong>Plan → Competition → Competitor Finder</strong>.</p><h2 id="competitors-ranked-by-competitive-strength" tabindex="-1"><strong>Competitors Ranked by Competitive Strength</strong> <a class="header-anchor" href="#competitors-ranked-by-competitive-strength" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;**Competitors Ranked by Competitive Strength**&quot;">​</a></h2><p>At the top of the page you&#39;ll find a quick summary that frames your competitive landscape at a glance:</p><ul><li><strong>Top threats</strong>: Competitors with a competition strength of 60 or higher — the shows competing most directly for your search rankings, audience, and platform visibility</li><li><strong>Rising competitors</strong>: Shows in the 35–59 strength range — moderate overlap in rankings, genre, or audience size that&#39;s worth keeping an eye on</li><li><strong>Keyword battlegrounds</strong>: The sum of observed keyword overlaps across competitors and platforms. The same keyword can count more than once, so this is not a count of distinct tracked keywords</li><li><strong>All competitors</strong>: A count of every competitor surfaced, ranked by relevance to your show. Competitor Finder shows up to 30 of the most relevant suggestions.</li></ul><p>Below the summary, each competitor appears as a card showing how many keywords you share, their visibility rank, and the platforms where they overlap with you. A badge in the corner helps you prioritize quickly:</p><ul><li><strong>HIGH</strong>: High competitive pressure — direct competition in search rankings and strong overlap with your topic</li><li><strong>MEDIUM</strong>: Medium competitive pressure — partial competition in search rankings and moderate topic overlap</li><li><strong>EMERGING</strong>: A show with limited keyword overlap so far. As you track more keywords, stronger competitors may appear.</li><li><strong>DUPLICATE</strong>: A possible additional listing of your own podcast. Check the listings and their identifiers before making changes; different platform listings do not necessarily mean you have a duplicate. If you are unsure which listing to keep, contact support. See <a href="/features/distribution-health.html">Distribution Health</a>.</li></ul><h2 id="tracking-a-competitor" tabindex="-1"><strong>Tracking a Competitor</strong> <a class="header-anchor" href="#tracking-a-competitor" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;**Tracking a Competitor**&quot;">​</a></h2><p>When you find a podcast worth monitoring, use the <strong>Track</strong> action on its card. Tracking adds the competitor to your <a href="/features/competitive-analysis.html">Competitive Analysis</a>, where you can follow their visibility, keyword overlap, and activity over time. Shows you already track are marked <strong>Tracking</strong>. The number of competitors you can track depends on your plan: Free tracks up to 2, Podcaster up to 4, Producer up to 25, and Agency is effectively unlimited.</p><p>If a show you want isn&#39;t in the suggestions, use <strong>Add competitor</strong> in Competitive Analysis to find it by name, Apple Podcasts or Spotify link, or RSS feed. Shows that are only listed in a non-US Apple Podcasts storefront can be added by pasting their Apple Podcasts link or ID.</p><h2 id="shows-on-the-same-apple-network" tabindex="-1"><strong>Shows on the Same Apple Network</strong> <a class="header-anchor" href="#shows-on-the-same-apple-network" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;**Shows on the Same Apple Network**&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Below your competitor cards, <strong>Same Apple network</strong> lists other shows that Apple Podcasts places on the same network (channel) as your show, such as a network or publisher page that groups several podcasts. Shows on one network often share promotion and audiences, so they can be worth tracking even when they share few keywords with you. The list shows the most recently active of these shows, leaves out your own show and the competitors you already track, and offers the same <strong>Track</strong> action. These shows are not ranked by keyword overlap, and being on the same network does not change any competition score.</p><p>If your show is not part of an Apple network, the section says so and stays empty. If PodSEO has not yet read your network from Apple, it says <strong>Not checked yet</strong>; this fills in with the next check of your Apple listing. The network itself is shown under <strong>Distribution → Appearance → Apple</strong>.</p><h2 id="when-strong-competitors-are-hard-to-find" tabindex="-1"><strong>When Strong Competitors Are Hard to Find</strong> <a class="header-anchor" href="#when-strong-competitors-are-hard-to-find" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;**When Strong Competitors Are Hard to Find**&quot;">​</a></h2><p>If your podcast is in a niche category or you&#39;re tracking only a few keywords, Competitor Finder may not find strong direct competitors right away. When that happens, it relaxes its filters and surfaces <strong>emerging competitors</strong> — podcasts with potential competitive relevance — and lets you know it has expanded the search. The best way to surface stronger competitors is to add more keywords for your show to compete on.</p><p>If no competitors meet the relevance threshold at all, you&#39;ll see options to <strong>Add more keywords</strong>, <strong>Refresh analysis</strong>, or <strong>Add competitor manually</strong> so you can broaden your search, try again, or start comparing against shows you already know.</p><h2 id="how-keyword-overlap-discovery-works" tabindex="-1"><strong>How Keyword Overlap Discovery Works</strong> <a class="header-anchor" href="#how-keyword-overlap-discovery-works" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;**How Keyword Overlap Discovery Works**&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="platform-specific-search-engine-analysis" tabindex="-1"><strong>Platform-Specific Search Engine Analysis</strong> <a class="header-anchor" href="#platform-specific-search-engine-analysis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;**Platform-Specific Search Engine Analysis**&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Search results and competing shows can differ across platforms. <a href="https://podcasters.apple.com/support/3686-search-on-apple-podcasts" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Apple</a> names show and channel names, episode titles, popularity, and engagement from search among its factors. <a href="https://creators.spotify.com/resources/podcast-seo" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Spotify</a> recommends clear titles and descriptions and reviewing transcripts and chapters. Neither source publishes a complete ranking formula or weights. Compare observed results rather than assuming why a particular show ranks.</p><h3 id="understanding-keyword-overlap" tabindex="-1"><strong>Understanding Keyword Overlap</strong> <a class="header-anchor" href="#understanding-keyword-overlap" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;**Understanding Keyword Overlap**&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Competitor Finder analyzes which podcasts appear in search results for the same keywords as your podcast, showing you:</p><ul><li><strong>Direct Keyword Competition</strong>: Podcasts ranking for your exact target keywords</li><li><strong>Search Result Proximity</strong>: Shows appearing near your podcast in search results</li><li><strong>Platform Variations</strong>: How competitor sets differ across Apple Podcasts, Spotify, Amazon Music, and YouTube Music</li><li><strong>Ranking Performance</strong>: Which competitors consistently outrank you for shared keywords</li></ul><h2 id="why-different-search-engines-matter" tabindex="-1"><strong>Why Different Search Engines Matter</strong> <a class="header-anchor" href="#why-different-search-engines-matter" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;**Why Different Search Engines Matter**&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="search-algorithm-variations-create-different-competitive-landscapes" tabindex="-1"><strong>Search Algorithm Variations Create Different Competitive Landscapes</strong> <a class="header-anchor" href="#search-algorithm-variations-create-different-competitive-landscapes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;**Search Algorithm Variations Create Different Competitive Landscapes**&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Understanding that each platform has distinct search behavior is crucial for effective competitor analysis:</p><ul><li><strong>Platform differences</strong>: A show may appear for a term on one platform but not another. Compare the same term and country where available.</li><li><strong>Search and recommendations</strong>: Search results and personalized recommendations are different discovery surfaces; do not assume they use identical signals.</li></ul><h3 id="strategic-keyword-overlap-analysis" tabindex="-1"><strong>Strategic Keyword Overlap Analysis</strong> <a class="header-anchor" href="#strategic-keyword-overlap-analysis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;**Strategic Keyword Overlap Analysis**&quot;">​</a></h3><p>For each platform, Competitor Finder shows you:</p><ol><li><strong>Show Keyword Competitors</strong>: Podcasts ranking in the top positions for your main target keywords</li><li><strong>Related Keyword Overlap</strong>: Shows competing for related terms that could expand your visibility</li><li><strong>Ranking Gap Analysis</strong>: Identifies competitors consistently outranking you for shared keywords</li><li><strong>Platform-Specific Opportunities</strong>: Keywords where you face different competition levels across platforms</li></ol><h3 id="competitor-selection-based-on-keyword-performance" tabindex="-1"><strong>Competitor Selection Based on Keyword Performance</strong> <a class="header-anchor" href="#competitor-selection-based-on-keyword-performance" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;**Competitor Selection Based on Keyword Performance**&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Focus on competitors who:</p><ul><li><strong>Consistently Outrank You</strong>: For keywords where you want to improve position</li><li><strong>Target Similar Keywords</strong>: Shows competing for the same search terms</li><li><strong>Excel on Specific Platforms</strong>: Where they rank better than you for shared keywords</li><li><strong>Gap Opportunities</strong>: Where they rank well but you don&#39;t appear at all</li></ul><h2 id="leveraging-keyword-overlap-intelligence" tabindex="-1"><strong>Leveraging Keyword Overlap Intelligence</strong> <a class="header-anchor" href="#leveraging-keyword-overlap-intelligence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;**Leveraging Keyword Overlap Intelligence**&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="cross-platform-competitive-strategy" tabindex="-1"><strong>Cross-Platform Competitive Strategy</strong> <a class="header-anchor" href="#cross-platform-competitive-strategy" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;**Cross-Platform Competitive Strategy**&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Once you identify competitors through keyword overlap, use this intelligence strategically:</p><ul><li><strong>Platform-Specific Optimization</strong>: Compare where competitors rank on each platform and use the differences to identify opportunities to investigate</li><li><strong>Keyword Gap Analysis</strong>: Identify keywords where competitors rank well but you don&#39;t appear, revealing expansion opportunities</li><li><strong>Content Strategy Insights</strong>: Analyze how competitors structure titles and descriptions to rank for shared keywords</li><li><strong>Platform Prioritization</strong>: Focus optimization efforts on platforms where you face the weakest keyword competition</li></ul><h3 id="understanding-competitive-keyword-patterns" tabindex="-1"><strong>Understanding Competitive Keyword Patterns</strong> <a class="header-anchor" href="#understanding-competitive-keyword-patterns" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;**Understanding Competitive Keyword Patterns**&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Track how keyword overlap changes over time:</p><ul><li><strong>Seasonal Variations</strong>: Some competitors may rank better for certain keywords during specific periods</li><li><strong>Content Strategy Impact</strong>: Monitor how competitor metadata changes affect their keyword rankings</li><li><strong>New Competitor Emergence</strong>: Regular keyword overlap analysis reveals new podcasts entering your competitive space</li><li><strong>Platform Algorithm Updates</strong>: Changes in search engine behavior can shift your competitive landscape</li></ul><h2 id="best-practices-for-keyword-based-competitor-analysis" tabindex="-1"><strong>Best Practices for Keyword-Based Competitor Analysis</strong> <a class="header-anchor" href="#best-practices-for-keyword-based-competitor-analysis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;**Best Practices for Keyword-Based Competitor Analysis**&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="platform-by-platform-analysis" tabindex="-1"><strong>Platform-by-Platform Analysis</strong> <a class="header-anchor" href="#platform-by-platform-analysis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;**Platform-by-Platform Analysis**&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li><strong>Apple Podcasts</strong>: Compare clear, specific show and episode titles; Apple identifies these as search metadata.</li><li><strong>Spotify</strong>: Review relevant titles and descriptions alongside Spotify&#39;s creator guidance.</li><li><strong>Amazon Music and YouTube Music</strong>: Compare observed results for your terms without assuming undisclosed ranking factors.</li></ul><h3 id="strategic-competitor-selection" tabindex="-1"><strong>Strategic Competitor Selection</strong> <a class="header-anchor" href="#strategic-competitor-selection" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;**Strategic Competitor Selection**&quot;">​</a></h3><ul><li><strong>Keyword Relevance First</strong>: Prioritize competitors ranking for your most important target keywords</li><li><strong>Platform Performance</strong>: Track competitors who consistently outrank you on specific platforms</li><li><strong>Ranking Consistency</strong>: Focus on competitors who maintain strong keyword positions over time</li><li><strong>Growth Patterns</strong>: Monitor competitors showing improvement in keyword rankings to learn from their strategies</li></ul><h2 id="maximizing-keyword-overlap-insights" tabindex="-1"><strong>Maximizing Keyword Overlap Insights</strong> <a class="header-anchor" href="#maximizing-keyword-overlap-insights" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;**Maximizing Keyword Overlap Insights**&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="competitive-intelligence-through-search-performance" tabindex="-1"><strong>Competitive Intelligence Through Search Performance</strong> <a class="header-anchor" href="#competitive-intelligence-through-search-performance" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;**Competitive Intelligence Through Search Performance**&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Use keyword overlap data to inform your optimization strategy:</p><ul><li><strong>Title Optimization</strong>: Learn from competitor titles that rank well for shared keywords</li><li><strong>Description Strategies</strong>: Analyze how top-ranking competitors structure their descriptions</li><li><strong>Category Selection</strong>: Compare relevant categories for browsing and charts without assuming they determine keyword rankings</li><li><strong>Content Themes</strong>: Identify keyword patterns that suggest successful content strategies</li></ul><hr><p><strong>Next Steps</strong>: Use your keyword overlap analysis to inform your Keyword Strategy and track competitor performance in the Competitive Analysis feature. This search-focused intelligence helps you make data-driven decisions about where to compete and how to optimize for better keyword rankings across all platforms.</p>',53)])])}const y=t(s,[["render",n]]);export{m as __pageData,y as default};
